WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.582 --> 00:00:02.908
- Before I went to college, I
wish I had hugged my parents

00:00:02.908 --> 00:00:05.432
and ate a lot more of
their home cooked meals

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:09.599
because you're gonna get
tired of ramen pretty quick.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.828
- First off, don't worry about
any of the high school drama

00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:19.733
and any of the guys in your
high school, any of those people

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.085
because they're gonna be
irrelevant in about two months.

00:00:22.085 --> 00:00:23.383
- The one thing I wish I would have done

00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:25.315
in between high school and college

00:00:25.315 --> 00:00:27.190
would definitely be find internships,

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.968
at least one summer internship

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.094
or just internships at all.

00:00:31.094 --> 00:00:32.705
Start the free stuff now

00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:34.138
so that once you leave college,

00:00:34.138 --> 00:00:35.645
you've already built your ground

00:00:35.645 --> 00:00:38.730
and most jobs actually want
to hire you afterwards.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.132
- I'm from Hawaii,

00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:42.767
and something that I
really wish I did more of

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:46.049
before I went to college
was go to the beach.

00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:49.196
I went to school in Ohio,
in middle of nowhere Ohio,

00:00:49.196 --> 00:00:51.015
and so, obviously there are no beaches

00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:53.002
and the closest body of
water was the Ohio River

00:00:53.002 --> 00:00:55.370
so that's not the best to swim in.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.789
- Learn about sex and drugs

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.759
because there's a lot of that in college

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.569
and it's better to be educated.

00:01:01.569 --> 00:01:03.816
That way, you know what
you're getting yourself into.

00:01:03.816 --> 00:01:05.826
You're not doing too much too fast.

00:01:05.826 --> 00:01:07.543
- Remember to document everything.

00:01:07.543 --> 00:01:09.743
Take as many pictures with
your friends as possible.

00:01:09.743 --> 00:01:11.279
- Get that wardrobe right.

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:13.717
You gotta go in, you
gotta stunt on everyone,

00:01:13.717 --> 00:01:14.762
you gotta be looking good,

00:01:14.762 --> 00:01:17.139
so just kind of like
revitalize that whole wardrobe.

00:01:17.139 --> 00:01:19.218
- Learn some respect for deadlines.

00:01:19.218 --> 00:01:21.353
That shit's gonna get you.

00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:22.807
If you don't get it,

00:01:22.807 --> 00:01:24.862
they're gonna smack you against the wall.

00:01:24.862 --> 00:01:27.022
Do that and learn how to cook.

00:01:27.022 --> 00:01:28.824
- You should thank your teachers.

00:01:28.824 --> 00:01:30.581
You should also hang out with your friends

00:01:30.581 --> 00:01:31.511
as much as possible.

00:01:31.511 --> 00:01:33.239
It's the last summer you're
gonna be able to do it.

00:01:33.239 --> 00:01:36.252
- Somehow, remember that you
signed off on a student loan

00:01:36.252 --> 00:01:38.281
'cause you're gonna forget

00:01:38.281 --> 00:01:39.822
and then, five years later,

00:01:39.822 --> 00:01:41.056
you're gonna get something in the mail

00:01:41.056 --> 00:01:43.443
that says you signed a
student loan for like $5000.

00:01:43.443 --> 00:01:45.360
Totally not speaking
from personal experience.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.570
- Read a book that you
actually want to read for fun

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:49.554
because I don't think you're gonna

00:01:49.554 --> 00:01:50.589
want to read a book for fun

00:01:50.589 --> 00:01:53.613
for the next four years
until college is over.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:57.471
- My last summer before
college, I definitely regret

00:01:57.471 --> 00:01:59.769
not actually just chilling.

00:01:59.769 --> 00:02:03.114
I was just doing too much
and preparing for college.

00:02:03.114 --> 00:02:04.960
And then once it starts, that's it.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.162
You go through your four years,

00:02:06.162 --> 00:02:09.262
and then it's like you're in
the workforce and that's that.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.561
- Before I went to college,
I worked at my summer camp,

00:02:11.561 --> 00:02:15.190
my sleep away summer camp,
and I didn't pack anything.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.090
And my mom graciously packed

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.624
everything I could have
ever needed for me,

00:02:19.624 --> 00:02:22.729
so my advice is to go get things

00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:24.317
you need for college for yourself

00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:26.705
so that when you get there,
you know what you have.

00:02:26.705 --> 00:02:28.147
- During my last summer before college,

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:29.978
I wish I would have
threw a graduation party.

00:02:29.978 --> 00:02:32.529
I'm 25 and I never had a big party that

00:02:32.529 --> 00:02:34.252
celebrated me and my accomplishments,

00:02:34.252 --> 00:02:35.423
so that would have been dope.

00:02:35.423 --> 00:02:36.256
- Take risks.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.662
Put yourself in uncomfortable situations.

00:02:37.662 --> 00:02:39.377
Don't do what everyone's telling you to do

00:02:39.377 --> 00:02:41.071
'cause at least in my life,

00:02:41.071 --> 00:02:44.286
that's when I found the
most interesting things

00:02:44.286 --> 00:02:46.567
and kind of discovered who I was.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.234
- Don't drink Jager.

